.TH HOMED 8 "October 2026" "homed 0.2.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
homed \- NSS-backed org.freedesktop.home1 D-Bus and Varlink compatibility service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B homed
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B homed
provides a limited, non-systemd implementation of the
.BR org.freedesktop.home1
D-Bus API and the
.BR io.systemd.UserDatabase
Varlink interface for accounts visible through the system's Name Service Switch (NSS).
The D-Bus service owns the system-bus name
.BR org.freedesktop.home1
and exports the manager object at
.BR /org/freedesktop/home1 .
The Varlink service listens on
.I /run/systemd/userdb/io.systemd.Home
so compatible user-database clients can discover it.
The daemon is intended as a compatibility layer for systems such as Slackware
that do not use systemd.
.PP
This release is not a full replacement for systemd-homed. It reads account
information from NSS/passwd and does not create or manage home storage, perform
encryption, or activate login sessions. The daemon currently requires root.
.SH VARLINK METHODS
The Varlink interface implements
.BR GetUserRecord ,
.BR GetGroupRecord ,
and
.BR GetMemberships .
The first two return NSS-derived user or group records and set
.B incomplete
to true because NSS does not supply managed-home metadata. Membership queries
return the user/group pairs known through NSS. Unsupported enumeration requests
return
.BR io.systemd.UserDatabase.EnumerationNotSupported .
The Varlink socket is created with mode 0666 for user-database discovery
clients; access to it does not enable home-management operations.
.SH MANAGER METHODS
The manager object currently implements these methods:
.TP
.B GetHomeByName(user_name)
Looks up an NSS account by name and returns its UID, state, GID, real name,
home directory, shell, and per-home object path.
.TP
.B GetHomeByUID(uid)
Looks up an NSS account by numeric UID and returns its name, state, GID, real
name, home directory, shell, and per-home object path.
.TP
.B ListHomes()
Returns the NSS-visible accounts and their basic account information. These
entries represent NSS accounts, not necessarily managed home areas.
.TP
.B GetUserRecordByName(user_name)
Returns a user-record dictionary derived from NSS fields.
.TP
.B GetUserRecordByUID(uid)
Returns a user-record dictionary for the specified UID.
.TP
.B GetUserRecordByPID(pid)
Reads the real UID from the process status file under
.I /proc
and returns the corresponding NSS user record.
.PP
The user-record dictionary currently includes
.BR userName ,
.BR uid ,
.BR gid ,
.BR realName ,
.BR homeDirectory ,
.BR shell ,
.BR service ,
and
.BR disposition .
The D-Bus interface reports service
.BR nss ;
the Varlink interface identifies its provider as
.BR io.systemd.Home .
These records return true for the
.I incomplete
output because NSS does not provide managed-home metadata, secrets, bindings,
or signatures required for a complete systemd-homed user record.
.TP
.B AutoLogin
The manager exposes this read-only property as an empty array.
.SH PER-HOME OBJECTS
Each NSS account discovered by the daemon is represented at
.BR /org/freedesktop/home1/home/_UID ,
where
.I UID
is the account's numeric UID.
The
.B org.freedesktop.home1.Home
interface exposes read-only account properties. Its lifecycle methods currently
return
.B org.freedesktop.home1.NotSupported
because managed storage and lifecycle operations have not been implemented.
.SH D-BUS REGISTRATION AND LOGGING
At startup the daemon logs successful registration of the manager object.
If it loses or cannot acquire its D-Bus name, it schedules a retry after 2500
milliseconds. Messages are sent through syslog under the
.B homed
identifier and are handled by the system's configured logging service.
.SH EXAMPLES
Inspect the manager interface:
.PP
.nf
busctl --system introspect org.freedesktop.home1 /org/freedesktop/home1
.fi
.PP
Look up an account through Varlink:
.PP
.nf
varlink call unix:/run/systemd/userdb/io.systemd.Home io.systemd.UserDatabase.GetUserRecord '{"userName":"root","service":"io.systemd.Home"}'
.fi
.SH LIMITATIONS
.B homed
does not implement home creation or registration, storage backends, encrypted
home images, activation/deactivation, locking/unlocking, resizing, home removal,
full record parsing or validation, or Polkit-enforced authorization for
management operations. Do not rely on it to provide systemd-homed storage or
login-activation semantics.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/homed
Typical installed daemon path; the actual path depends on the Meson
.B libexecdir
setting.
.TP
.I /run/systemd/userdb/io.systemd.Home
Varlink socket used for user-database discovery.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dbus-1/interfaces/org.freedesktop.home1.xml
Installed D-Bus interface description; the actual path depends on the Meson
.B datadir
setting.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR busctl (1),
.BR varlink (1),
.BR dbus-daemon (1),
.BR nsswitch.conf (5)
